/-!
# Integral domination of an fppf covering of an arbitrary scheme

[Stacks, Tag 0CNZ] states that an fppf covering of a scheme is dominated by a single surjective
*integral* morphism which, on a Zariski covering of its source, factors through members of the
given covering. `StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Topologies.V.FppfIntegralDomination` proves it
for a quasi-separated base. This file proves it for an **arbitrary** base, from one hypothesis:
`AlgebraicGeometry.HasFiniteLocalSections`.

## The hypothesis, and why it is this one and not [Stacks, Tag 0CNX]

The Stacks proof of Tag 0CNZ applies Tag 0CNX — the extension of a surjective integral
morphism from an open subscheme — twice, at an arbitrary member of an open covering. Tag 0CNX
as printed is **false**: the base change it asks for forces the extended algebra to be
generated by global sections, and over a non-retrocompact open it need not be. So the
quasi-separatedness of the base cannot be removed by proving Tag 0CNX.

What the proof of Tag 0CNZ actually consumes is weaker, and is isolated here as
`AlgebraicGeometry.HasFiniteLocalSections`: a *finite locally free* surjective morphism over an
*affine* open `Ω` of a base `Y`, around a point `y` of `Ω`, is **locally sectioned** over some
surjective integral cover of `Y` — not recovered by base change from it. Four features make
this the right hypothesis.

* It asks for a morphism to the cover and not an isomorphism onto the base change, so it is a
  statement about germs. In particular it survives replacing `Y` by a closed subscheme, which
  the base-change statement does not: the only closed subscheme through which the construction
  can be routed is the *reduced* one on the closure of `Ω`, whose intersection with `Ω` is
  `Ω` reduced and not `Ω`.
* It asks only for points over the single point `y`, so the affine open `Ω` may be shrunk
  around `y` at will.
* It asks it of a *finite locally free* morphism, which is what [Stacks, Tag 05WN] supplies at
  both places the Stacks proof applies Tag 0CNX. Together with the previous point this means
  the algebra to be extended may be assumed free over the sections of the affine open.
* It asks for an *affine* open on which the section lives, which is what lets the hypothesis be
  applied a second time, now over the integral cover it has just produced.

## Main results

* `AlgebraicGeometry.HasFiniteLocalSections` is the hypothesis, and
  `AlgebraicGeometry.hasFiniteLocalSections` proves it.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.hasFiniteLocalSections_of_forall_integral_surjective_extension` shows it
  asks for no more than [Stacks, Tag 0CNX] as printed does.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.hasFiniteLocalSections_of_dense` reduces it to the case of a *reduced*
  base in which the affine open is *dense*, which is the case in which a section over the open
  has a well-defined ideal of denominators.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.exists_integralChart_of_hasFiniteLocalSections` is the per-point heart:
  at a point of an arbitrary base, the chart data produced by [Stacks, Tag 05WN] is shrunk to an
  affine neighbourhood and sectioned, once.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.exists_integral_surjective_refinement_of_hasFiniteLocalSections` is
  [Stacks, Tag 0CNZ] for an arbitrary base, granted
  `AlgebraicGeometry.HasQuasiFiniteSlices` ([Stacks, Tag 0570]) and
  `AlgebraicGeometry.HasFiniteLocalSections`.

## Implementation notes

Nothing in this file is tagged: every result is conditional on two hypotheses that this library
does not prove. The tag registration for 0CNZ stays on
`AlgebraicGeometry.exists_integral_surjective_openCover_factorization_of_mem_fppfPrecoverage`,
which is unconditional and restricted to a quasi-separated base.

The construction is the Stacks one with both applications of Tag 0CNX replaced by
`AlgebraicGeometry.HasFiniteLocalSections`, and it is shorter for it: where the extension
produced an open subscheme of a cover and a morphism had to be lifted through it, a section is
already a morphism, and the chart of the source is the preimage of the open the section lives
on. The two levels of products — over the points of the first cover lying over the chosen
point, then over the points of the base — are unchanged, and are
`AlgebraicGeometry.hasProduct_of_isAffineHom` together with [Stacks, Tags 0CNJ, 0CNK].

No smallness is imposed on the index type of the given covering: [Stacks, Tag 05WN] accepts a
family indexed in any universe and the products taken here are indexed by points of schemes.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 0CNZ](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0CNZ)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0CNX](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0CNX)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 05WN](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/05WN)
-/

@[expose] public section

open CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Limits TopologicalSpace

universe u v w

namespace AlgebraicGeometry

/-- **Local sections of a finite locally free morphism over an affine open.** For every scheme
`Y`, every point `y` of `Y`, every affine open `Ω` containing `y` and every finite locally free
surjective morphism `π : Z ⟶ Ω` there is a surjective integral morphism `a : A ⟶ Y` such that
every point of `A` lying over `y` has an affine open neighbourhood `V` in `A` carrying a
morphism `V ⟶ Z` over `Y`.

This is what the proof of [Stacks, Tag 0CNZ] uses [Stacks, Tag 0CNX] for, and unlike Tag 0CNX
it is not refuted by
`AlgebraicGeometry.exists_isIntegralHom_surjective_not_baseChange`: nothing is asserted to be
a base change, the morphism `v` is only a section of `Z ×_Ω V ⟶ V`. -/
def HasFiniteLocalSections : Prop :=
  ∀ (Y : Scheme.{u}) (y : Y) (Ω : Y.Opens), IsAffineOpen Ω → y ∈ Ω →
    ∀ (Z : Scheme.{u}) (π : Z ⟶ Ω.toScheme), Stacks.Morphisms.IsFiniteLocallyFree π →
      Surjective π →
      ∃ (A : Scheme.{u}) (a : A ⟶ Y), IsIntegralHom a ∧ Surjective a ∧
        ∀ α : A, a.base α = y → ∃ V : A.Opens, IsAffineOpen V ∧ α ∈ V ∧
          ∃ v : V.toScheme ⟶ Z, v ≫ π ≫ Ω.ι = V.ι ≫ a

/-- **The hypothesis is weaker than [Stacks, Tag 0CNX] as printed.** If a surjective integral
morphism over an *arbitrary* open subscheme extended to one over the whole scheme — which is
what the source asserts, and what
`AlgebraicGeometry.not_forall_exists_integral_surjective_extension` refutes — then
`AlgebraicGeometry.HasFiniteLocalSections` would hold.

The section is the inverse of the open immersion the extension produces, which is an
isomorphism onto an *affine* open because a scheme finite over an affine one is affine; its
image is the preimage of `Ω`, so it contains every point lying over `y`. So nothing is asked
for here that the source does not already claim. -/
theorem hasFiniteLocalSections_of_forall_integral_surjective_extension
    (H : ∀ (Y : Scheme.{u}) (Ω : Y.Opens) (Z : Scheme.{u}) (π : Z ⟶ Ω.toScheme),
      IsIntegralHom π → Surjective π →
      ∃ (A : Scheme.{u}) (a : A ⟶ Y), IsIntegralHom a ∧ Surjective a ∧
        ∃ d : Z ⟶ A, IsOpenImmersion d ∧ d ≫ a = π ≫ Ω.ι ∧
          Set.range d.base = (a ⁻¹ᵁ Ω : Set A)) :
    HasFiniteLocalSections.{u} := by
  intro Y y Ω hΩ hy Z π hπflf hπsurj
  have : IsFinite π :=
    ((Stacks.Morphisms.isFiniteLocallyFree_iff_isFinite_flat_locallyOfFinitePresentation
      π).mp hπflf).1
  have : Surjective π := hπsurj
  have hΩaff : IsAffine Ω.toScheme := hΩ
  have hZaff : IsAffine Z := isAffine_of_isAffineHom π
  obtain ⟨A, a, haint, hasurj, d, hdopen, hdcomp, hdrange⟩ :=
    H Y Ω Z π inferInstance inferInstance
  have : IsOpenImmersion d := hdopen
  refine ⟨A, a, haint, hasurj, fun α hα => ?_⟩
  have hαmem : α ∈ d.opensRange := by
    change α ∈ Set.range d.base
    rw [hdrange]
    change a.base α ∈ Ω
    rw [hα]
    exact hy
  refine ⟨d.opensRange, isAffineOpen_opensRange d, hαmem, d.isoOpensRange.inv, ?_⟩
  rw [← hdcomp, ← Category.assoc, Scheme.Hom.isoOpensRange_inv_comp]

/-! ### Reduction to a reduced base in which the affine open is dense -/

/-- The **dense case** of `AlgebraicGeometry.HasFiniteLocalSections`: the base is reduced, and
the affine open is dense in it.

This is the case in which restriction of sections to the open subscheme is injective, so that
a section over the open has a well-defined ideal of denominators; the general case reduces to
it by `AlgebraicGeometry.hasFiniteLocalSections_of_dense`. -/
def HasFiniteLocalSectionsOfDense : Prop :=
  ∀ (Y : Scheme.{u}), IsReduced Y → ∀ (y : Y) (Ω : Y.Opens), IsAffineOpen Ω → y ∈ Ω →
    Dense (Ω : Set Y) →
    ∀ (Z : Scheme.{u}) (π : Z ⟶ Ω.toScheme), Stacks.Morphisms.IsFiniteLocallyFree π →
      Surjective π →
      ∃ (A : Scheme.{u}) (a : A ⟶ Y), IsIntegralHom a ∧ Surjective a ∧
        ∀ α : A, a.base α = y → ∃ V : A.Opens, IsAffineOpen V ∧ α ∈ V ∧
          ∃ v : V.toScheme ⟶ Z, v ≫ π ≫ Ω.ι = V.ι ≫ a

/-- If a closed immersion has as image the closure of an open subset `Ω` of the target, then
the preimage of `Ω` is dense in its source: the image of the closure of that preimage is closed
and contains `Ω`, hence is the whole image. -/
lemma dense_preimage_of_range_eq_closure {Y' Y : Scheme.{u}} (ι : Y' ⟶ Y) [IsClosedImmersion ι]
    {Ω : Y.Opens} (hr : Set.range ι.base = closure (Ω : Set Y)) :
    Dense ((ι ⁻¹ᵁ Ω : Y'.Opens) : Set Y') := by
  have hemb := IsClosedImmersion.isClosedEmbedding ι
  have h1 : (ι.base : Y' → Y) '' (ι.base ⁻¹' (Ω : Set Y)) = (Ω : Set Y) := by
    rw [Set.image_preimage_eq_inter_range, hr, Set.inter_eq_left]
    exact subset_closure
  have h2 : closure ((ι.base : Y' → Y) '' (ι.base ⁻¹' (Ω : Set Y)))
      = (ι.base : Y' → Y) '' closure (ι.base ⁻¹' (Ω : Set Y)) := hemb.closure_image_eq _
  rw [h1] at h2
  rw [show ((ι ⁻¹ᵁ Ω : Y'.Opens) : Set Y') = ι.base ⁻¹' (Ω : Set Y) from rfl,
    dense_iff_closure_eq]
  refine hemb.injective.image_injective ?_
  rw [← h2, Set.image_univ, hr]

/-- The base change of a surjective finite locally free morphism is again one. -/
private theorem exists_pullback_isFiniteLocallyFree {X Y Z : Scheme.{u}} (g : X ⟶ Y)
    (hg : Stacks.Morphisms.IsFiniteLocallyFree g) (hs : Surjective g) (θ : Z ⟶ Y) :
    ∃ (P : Scheme.{u}) (pr : P ⟶ X) (q : P ⟶ Z), pr ≫ g = q ≫ θ ∧
      Stacks.Morphisms.IsFiniteLocallyFree q ∧ Surjective q := by
  obtain ⟨h₁, h₂, h₃⟩ :=
    (Stacks.Morphisms.isFiniteLocallyFree_iff_isFinite_flat_locallyOfFinitePresentation g).mp hg
  have := h₁
  have := h₂
  have := h₃
  exact ⟨pullback g θ, pullback.fst _ _, pullback.snd _ _, pullback.condition,
    (Stacks.Morphisms.isFiniteLocallyFree_iff_isFinite_flat_locallyOfFinitePresentation
      _).mpr ⟨inferInstance, inferInstance, inferInstance⟩, inferInstance⟩

/-- A point of `W` mapping into the image of an open immersion `f : U ⟶ S` has an affine open
neighbourhood whose inclusion into `S` factors through `U`. -/
private theorem exists_isAffineOpen_lift {S U W : Scheme.{u}} (f : U ⟶ S) [IsOpenImmersion f]
    (g : W ⟶ S) (w : W) (hw : g.base w ∈ Set.range f.base) :
    ∃ Θ : W.Opens, IsAffineOpen Θ ∧ w ∈ Θ ∧ ∃ θ : Θ.toScheme ⟶ U, θ ≫ f = Θ.ι ≫ g := by
  obtain ⟨-, ⟨Θ, hΘ, rfl⟩, h₁, h₂⟩ := W.isBasis_affineOpens.exists_subset_of_mem_open
    (show w ∈ (g ⁻¹ᵁ f.opensRange : Set W) from hw) (g ⁻¹ᵁ f.opensRange).2
  exact ⟨Θ, hΘ, h₁,
    IsOpenImmersion.lift f (Scheme.Opens.ι Θ ≫ g) (by rintro - ⟨p, rfl⟩; exact h₂ p.2),
    IsOpenImmersion.lift_fac _ _ _⟩

/-- The product of a family of integral surjective morphisms to `S` is integral and surjective
over `S`, with projections compatible with the structure morphisms. -/
private theorem exists_integral_surjective_product {I : Type u} {S : Scheme.{u}}
    {T : I → Scheme.{u}} (f : ∀ i, T i ⟶ S) (hint : ∀ i, IsIntegralHom (f i))
    (hsurj : ∀ i, Surjective (f i)) :
    ∃ (P : Scheme.{u}) (g : P ⟶ S), IsIntegralHom g ∧ Surjective g ∧
      ∃ p : ∀ i, P ⟶ T i, ∀ i, p i ≫ f i = g := by
  have := hint
  have := hsurj
  have := hasProduct_of_isAffineHom S T f
  exact ⟨(∏ᶜ (fun i => Over.mk (f i))).left, (∏ᶜ (fun i => Over.mk (f i))).hom,
    isIntegralHom_product S T f, surjective_product_hom S T f,
    fun i => (Pi.π (fun i => Over.mk (f i)) i).left,
    fun i => by simpa using Over.w (Pi.π (fun i => Over.mk (f i)) i)⟩

/-- **The reduction.** The dense case of the hypothesis implies the hypothesis.

Let `Ω` be an affine open of a scheme `Y` and `y` a point of `Ω`. Let `Y'` be the reduced
closed subscheme on the closure of `Ω` and `Y''` the reduced closed subscheme on the closed
complement of `Ω`. Then `Y' ⨿ Y'' ⟶ Y` is surjective and integral, and no point of `Y''` lies
over `y`; inside `Y'` the open `Ω` is reduced and dense, and the given morphism is replaced by
its base change along `Ω ∩ Y' ⟶ Ω`, whose sections compose with the closed immersion back into
the original.

This is the step that a *base-change* statement would not survive, and the reason
`AlgebraicGeometry.HasFiniteLocalSections` is phrased with a morphism instead: the intersection
of `Ω` with `Y'` is `Ω` reduced, not `Ω`, so a cover recovered by base change from a cover of
`Y'` restricts over `Ω` to the base change of the given morphism and not to it. -/
theorem hasFiniteLocalSections_of_dense (H : HasFiniteLocalSectionsOfDense.{u}) :
    HasFiniteLocalSections.{u} := by
  intro Y y Ω hΩ hy Z π hπflf hπsurj
  -- The reduced closed subscheme on the closure of `Ω`, and the one on its complement.
  set IY := Scheme.IdealSheafData.vanishingIdeal
    (⟨closure (Ω : Set Y), isClosed_closure⟩ : Closeds Y) with hIY
  set IZ := Scheme.IdealSheafData.vanishingIdeal
    (⟨(Ω : Set Y)ᶜ, Ω.isOpen.isClosed_compl⟩ : Closeds Y) with hIZ
  set Y' := IY.subscheme with hY'
  set Y'' := IZ.subscheme with hY''
  set ιY : Y' ⟶ Y := IY.subschemeι with hιYdef
  set ιZ : Y'' ⟶ Y := IZ.subschemeι with hιZdef
  have hY'range : Set.range ιY.base = closure (Ω : Set Y) :=
    Scheme.IdealSheafData.range_subschemeι_vanishingIdeal _
  have hY''range : Set.range ιZ.base = (Ω : Set Y)ᶜ :=
    Scheme.IdealSheafData.range_subschemeι_vanishingIdeal _
  have hY'dense : Dense ((ιY ⁻¹ᵁ Ω : Y'.Opens) : Set Y') :=
    dense_preimage_of_range_eq_closure ιY hY'range
  -- A point of `Y'` over `y`, and the affine dense open `Ω'` of `Y'` it lies in.
  obtain ⟨y', hy'⟩ : y ∈ Set.range ιY.base := by
    rw [hY'range]; exact subset_closure hy
  have hy'mem : y' ∈ (ιY ⁻¹ᵁ Ω : Y'.Opens) := by
    change ιY.base y' ∈ Ω
    rw [hy']; exact hy
  have hΩ'aff : IsAffineOpen (ιY ⁻¹ᵁ Ω : Y'.Opens) := hΩ.preimage ιY
  -- The base change of the given morphism to `Ω'`.
  obtain ⟨Z', pr, π', hprcomm, hπ'flf, hπ'surj⟩ :=
    exists_pullback_isFiniteLocallyFree π hπflf hπsurj (ιY.resLE Ω (ιY ⁻¹ᵁ Ω) le_rfl)
  obtain ⟨A₀, a₀, ha₀int, ha₀surj, hsec⟩ :=
    H Y' inferInstance y' (ιY ⁻¹ᵁ Ω) hΩ'aff hy'mem hY'dense Z' π' hπ'flf hπ'surj
  have : IsIntegralHom a₀ := ha₀int
  have : Surjective a₀ := ha₀surj
  have : IsIntegralHom (a₀ ≫ ιY) := inferInstance
  refine ⟨A₀ ⨿ Y'', coprod.desc (a₀ ≫ ιY) ιZ, inferInstance, ⟨fun w => ?_⟩, fun α hα => ?_⟩
  · by_cases hw : w ∈ (Ω : Set Y)
    · obtain ⟨b, hb⟩ : w ∈ Set.range ιY.base := by
        rw [hY'range]; exact subset_closure hw
      obtain ⟨α₀, hα₀⟩ := ha₀surj.surj b
      refine ⟨(coprod.inl : A₀ ⟶ A₀ ⨿ Y'') α₀, ?_⟩
      rw [← Scheme.Hom.comp_apply, coprod.inl_desc, Scheme.Hom.comp_apply, hα₀, hb]
    · obtain ⟨c, hc⟩ : w ∈ Set.range ιZ.base := by
        rw [hY''range]; exact hw
      refine ⟨(coprod.inr : Y'' ⟶ A₀ ⨿ Y'') c, ?_⟩
      rw [← Scheme.Hom.comp_apply, coprod.inr_desc]
      exact hc
  · have hcov : Set.range (coprod.inl : A₀ ⟶ A₀ ⨿ Y'').base ∪
        Set.range (coprod.inr : Y'' ⟶ A₀ ⨿ Y'').base = Set.univ :=
      (isCompl_range_inl_inr A₀ Y'').sup_eq_top
    rcases hcov.ge (Set.mem_univ α) with ⟨α₀, rfl⟩ | ⟨c, rfl⟩
    · -- The point lies in the part over the closure of `Ω`, and over `y'`.
      rw [← Scheme.Hom.comp_apply, coprod.inl_desc] at hα
      have hα₀' : a₀.base α₀ = y' := by
        refine (IsClosedImmersion.isClosedEmbedding ιY).injective ?_
        rw [hy', ← Scheme.Hom.comp_apply]
        exact hα
      obtain ⟨V₀, hV₀aff, hα₀V₀, v₀, hv₀⟩ := hsec α₀ hα₀'
      have hV₀affine : IsAffine V₀.toScheme := hV₀aff
      refine ⟨(V₀.ι ≫ (coprod.inl : A₀ ⟶ A₀ ⨿ Y'')).opensRange,
        isAffineOpen_opensRange _, ⟨⟨α₀, hα₀V₀⟩, rfl⟩,
        (V₀.ι ≫ (coprod.inl : A₀ ⟶ A₀ ⨿ Y'')).isoOpensRange.inv ≫ v₀ ≫ pr, ?_⟩
      rw [← Scheme.Hom.isoOpensRange_inv_comp (V₀.ι ≫ (coprod.inl : A₀ ⟶ A₀ ⨿ Y''))]
      simp only [Category.assoc, coprod.inl_desc, reassoc_of% hprcomm,
        Scheme.Hom.resLE_comp_ι, reassoc_of% hv₀]
    · -- No point of the complement part lies over `y`, which is in `Ω`.
      exfalso
      have hmem : ιZ.base c ∈ (Ω : Set Y)ᶜ := by
        rw [← hY''range]; exact Set.mem_range_self c
      refine hmem ?_
      rw [← Scheme.Hom.comp_apply, coprod.inr_desc] at hα
      rw [hα]
      exact hy

/-- **The dense case of the hypothesis holds.** On a reduced scheme in which the affine open
`Ω` is dense, the algebra of denominators of a presentation of the sections of the finite
locally free morphism has a relative spectrum which is integral and surjective over the base
and which, over an affine open subset of `Ω`, carries a morphism to the source of the
morphism. -/
theorem hasFiniteLocalSectionsOfDense : HasFiniteLocalSectionsOfDense.{u} := by
  intro Y hYred y Ω hΩ hy hd Z π hflf hsurj
  have := hYred
  obtain ⟨D⟩ := Stacks.DenseDenominators.nonempty_sectionsData hΩ π hflf hsurj
  exact Stacks.DenseDenominators.exists_integralHom_surjective_section_of_sectionsData hd hΩ D
    y hy

/-- **The hypothesis holds.** Local sections of a finite locally free surjective morphism over
an affine open subset exist over a surjective integral cover of any scheme: the general case
reduces to the dense case by `AlgebraicGeometry.hasFiniteLocalSections_of_dense`. -/
theorem hasFiniteLocalSections : HasFiniteLocalSections.{u} :=
  hasFiniteLocalSections_of_dense hasFiniteLocalSectionsOfDense

/-- The per-point heart of [Stacks, Tag 0CNZ] for an arbitrary base.

Given the data that [Stacks, Tag 05WN] produces for an fppf covering `{f i}` of a scheme `S` —
an open cover `𝒰`, surjective finite locally free morphisms `g₁ j : W j ⟶ 𝒰.X j`, open covers
`𝒲 j` of the `W j`, surjective finite locally free morphisms `h₁ j k` onto their members, and
a factorization of each `T j k ⟶ S` through a member of the covering — every point `x` of `S`
has a surjective integral `a : A ⟶ S` such that every point of `A` over `x` lies in an affine
open `V` of `A` carrying a surjective *finite locally free* morphism from a scheme that still
maps to a member of the given covering, compatibly over `S`.

The chart `𝒰.X j` is shrunk to an affine open `Ω ∋ x`, `g₁ j` is replaced by its base change
along `Ω ⟶ 𝒰.X j`, and `AlgebraicGeometry.HasFiniteLocalSections` is applied to that base
change; the section is then shrunk until it lands in a single member of `𝒲 j`, and `h₁ j k` is
base changed along it. That the morphism produced is again finite locally free, and not merely
integral, is what lets the hypothesis be applied to it a second time. -/
theorem exists_integralChart_of_hasFiniteLocalSections (hLS : HasFiniteLocalSections.{u})
    {I : Type v} {S : Scheme.{u}}
    {X : I → Scheme.{u}} {f : ∀ i, X i ⟶ S}
    {𝒰 : S.OpenCover.{w}} {W : 𝒰.I₀ → Scheme.{u}} {g₁ : ∀ j, W j ⟶ 𝒰.X j}
    {𝒲 : ∀ j, (W j).OpenCover.{w}} {T : ∀ j, (𝒲 j).I₀ → Scheme.{u}}
    {h₁ : ∀ j k, T j k ⟶ (𝒲 j).X k}
    (hg₁ : ∀ j, Surjective (g₁ j))
    (hg₂ : ∀ j, Stacks.Morphisms.IsFiniteLocallyFree (g₁ j))
    (hh₁ : ∀ j k, Surjective (h₁ j k))
    (hh₂ : ∀ j k, Stacks.Morphisms.IsFiniteLocallyFree (h₁ j k))
    (hfac : ∀ j k, ∃ i, ∃ l : T j k ⟶ X i,
      l ≫ f i = h₁ j k ≫ (𝒲 j).f k ≫ g₁ j ≫ 𝒰.f j)
    (x : S) :
    ∃ (A : Scheme.{u}) (a : A ⟶ S), IsIntegralHom a ∧ Surjective a ∧
      ∀ α : A, a.base α = x → ∃ V : A.Opens, IsAffineOpen V ∧ α ∈ V ∧
        ∃ (T' : Scheme.{u}) (q : T' ⟶ V.toScheme),
          Stacks.Morphisms.IsFiniteLocallyFree q ∧ Surjective q ∧
          ∃ i, ∃ l : T' ⟶ X i, l ≫ f i = q ≫ V.ι ≫ a := by
  classical
  set j := 𝒰.idx x with hj
  obtain ⟨Ω, hΩaff, hxΩ, ι', hι'⟩ :=
    exists_isAffineOpen_lift (𝒰.f j) (𝟙 S) x (𝒰.covers x)
  rw [Category.comp_id] at hι'
  obtain ⟨Z, e, m, hZcomm, hmflf, hmsurj⟩ :=
    exists_pullback_isFiniteLocallyFree (g₁ j) (hg₂ j) (hg₁ j) ι'
  obtain ⟨A, a, haint, hasurj, hsec⟩ := hLS S x Ω hΩaff hxΩ Z m hmflf hmsurj
  refine ⟨A, a, haint, hasurj, fun α hα => ?_⟩
  obtain ⟨V, hVaff, hαV, v, hv⟩ := hsec α hα
  -- The section composed with `Z ⟶ W j`, and the member of `𝒲 j` it meets at `α`.
  set k := (𝒲 j).idx ((v ≫ e).base ⟨α, hαV⟩) with hk
  obtain ⟨Θ, hΘaff, hαΘ, θk, hθk⟩ :=
    exists_isAffineOpen_lift ((𝒲 j).f k) (v ≫ e) ⟨α, hαV⟩ ((𝒲 j).covers _)
  have hΘaffine : IsAffine Θ.toScheme := hΘaff
  obtain ⟨T₀, pr, q₀, hprcomm, hq₀flf, hq₀surj⟩ :=
    exists_pullback_isFiniteLocallyFree (h₁ j k) (hh₂ j k) (hh₁ j k) θk
  obtain ⟨hq₀fin, hq₀flat, hq₀lfp⟩ :=
    (Stacks.Morphisms.isFiniteLocallyFree_iff_isFinite_flat_locallyOfFinitePresentation
      q₀).mp hq₀flf
  have : IsFinite q₀ := hq₀fin
  have : Flat q₀ := hq₀flat
  have : LocallyOfFinitePresentation q₀ := hq₀lfp
  have : Surjective q₀ := hq₀surj
  refine ⟨(Θ.ι ≫ V.ι).opensRange,
    isAffineOpen_opensRange (Θ.ι ≫ V.ι), ⟨⟨⟨α, hαV⟩, hαΘ⟩, rfl⟩,
    T₀, q₀ ≫ (Θ.ι ≫ V.ι).isoOpensRange.hom,
    (Stacks.Morphisms.isFiniteLocallyFree_iff_isFinite_flat_locallyOfFinitePresentation
      _).mpr ⟨inferInstance, inferInstance, inferInstance⟩, inferInstance, ?_⟩
  obtain ⟨i, l, hl⟩ := hfac j k
  refine ⟨i, pr ≫ l, ?_⟩
  simp only [Category.assoc, hl, reassoc_of% hprcomm, reassoc_of% hθk, reassoc_of% hZcomm,
    hι', hv, Scheme.Hom.isoOpensRange_hom_ι_assoc]

/-- **[Stacks, Tag 0CNZ] for an arbitrary base**, granted [Stacks, Tag 0570] in the form
`AlgebraicGeometry.HasQuasiFiniteSlices` and `AlgebraicGeometry.HasFiniteLocalSections`: an
fppf covering of *any* scheme is dominated by a surjective integral morphism which, on a
Zariski covering of its source, factors through members of the given covering.

The quasi-separatedness that
`AlgebraicGeometry.exists_integral_surjective_refinement_of_mem_fppfPrecoverage` carries is
gone; what has taken its place is `AlgebraicGeometry.HasFiniteLocalSections`, which is applied
twice — once over `S` and once over the cover that produces — exactly where the Stacks proof
applies [Stacks, Tag 0CNX] twice.

This is not tagged: it is conditional on two hypotheses this library does not prove. -/
theorem exists_integral_surjective_refinement_of_hasFiniteLocalSections
    (h0570 : HasQuasiFiniteSlices.{u}) (hLS : HasFiniteLocalSections.{u})
    {I : Type v} {S : Scheme.{u}}
    (X : I → Scheme.{u}) (f : ∀ i, X i ⟶ S)
    (hf : Presieve.ofArrows X f ∈ Scheme.fppfPrecoverage S) :
    ∃ (S' : Scheme.{u}) (g : S' ⟶ S), IsIntegralHom g ∧ Surjective g ∧
      ∃ (J : Type u) (U : J → Scheme.{u}) (ι : ∀ c, U c ⟶ S'),
        Presieve.ofArrows U ι ∈ Scheme.zariskiPrecoverage S' ∧
          ∀ c, ∃ i, ∃ t : U c ⟶ X i, ι c ≫ g = t ≫ f i := by
  classical
  obtain ⟨𝒰, W, g₁, 𝒲, T, h₁, hg, hh, -, hfac⟩ :=
    Stacks.Topologies.Fppf.exists_openCover_finiteLocallyFree_refinement_of_hasQuasiFiniteSlices
      h0570 S { I₀ := I, X := X, f := f, mem₀ := hf }
  choose A a haint hasurj hV using
    exists_integralChart_of_hasFiniteLocalSections hLS (f := f)
      (fun j => (hg j).1) (fun j => (hg j).2) (fun j k => (hh j k).1)
      (fun j k => (hh j k).2) hfac
  choose V hVaff hVmem T' q hqflf hqsurj iIdx lMap hlMap using hV
  -- Section `q` over an integral cover of `A x`, by the hypothesis again.
  have hBex : ∀ (x : S) (α : A x) (hα : (a x).base α = x),
      ∃ (B : Scheme.{u}) (b : B ⟶ A x), IsIntegralHom b ∧ Surjective b ∧
        ∀ β : B, b.base β = α → ∃ V' : B.Opens, IsAffineOpen V' ∧ β ∈ V' ∧
          ∃ v : V'.toScheme ⟶ T' x α hα,
            v ≫ q x α hα ≫ (V x α hα).ι = V'.ι ≫ b := fun x α hα =>
    hLS (A x) α (V x α hα) (hVaff x α hα) (hVmem x α hα) (T' x α hα) (q x α hα)
      (hqflf x α hα) (hqsurj x α hα)
  choose B b hbint hbsurj hsec using hBex
  -- The product, over the points of `A x` lying over `x`, of those, in schemes over `A x`.
  choose C c hcint hcsurj pB hpB using fun x : S =>
    exists_integral_surjective_product (fun p : {α : A x // (a x).base α = x} => b x p.1 p.2)
      (fun p => hbint x p.1 p.2) (fun p => hbsurj x p.1 p.2)
  -- The product over the points of `S` of those, in schemes over `S`.
  obtain ⟨S', g, hgint, hgsurj, pC, hpC⟩ :=
    exists_integral_surjective_product (fun x : S => c x ≫ a x)
      (fun x => have := hcint x; have := haint x; inferInstance)
      (fun x => have := hcsurj x; have := hasurj x; inferInstance)
  -- Each point of `S'` lies over a point of `A (g z)` lying over `g z`, and over a point of the
  -- second cover of that.
  have hαover : ∀ z : S', (a (g.base z)).base ((pC (g.base z) ≫ c (g.base z)).base z)
      = g.base z := by
    intro z
    rw [← Scheme.Hom.comp_apply, Category.assoc, hpC (g.base z)]
  set idx : ∀ z : S', {α : A (g.base z) // (a (g.base z)).base α = g.base z} :=
    fun z => ⟨(pC (g.base z) ≫ c (g.base z)).base z, hαover z⟩ with hidx
  set φ : ∀ z : S', S' ⟶ B (g.base z) (idx z).1 (idx z).2 :=
    fun z => pC (g.base z) ≫ pB (g.base z) (idx z) with hφ
  have hφb : ∀ z : S', φ z ≫ b (g.base z) (idx z).1 (idx z).2
      = pC (g.base z) ≫ c (g.base z) := by
    intro z
    rw [hφ, Category.assoc, hpB]
  have hβover : ∀ z : S', (b (g.base z) (idx z).1 (idx z).2).base ((φ z).base z)
      = (idx z).1 := by
    intro z
    rw [← Scheme.Hom.comp_apply, hφb z]
  choose Vz hVzaff hVzmem vz hvz using
    fun z : S' => hsec (g.base z) (idx z).1 (idx z).2 ((φ z).base z) (hβover z)
  refine ⟨S', g, hgint, hgsurj, S',
    fun z => ((φ z) ⁻¹ᵁ Vz z).toScheme, fun z => ((φ z) ⁻¹ᵁ Vz z).ι, ?_, ?_⟩
  · rw [Scheme.ofArrows_mem_precoverage_iff (P := @IsOpenImmersion)]
    refine ⟨fun z => ⟨z, ?_⟩, fun z => inferInstance⟩
    rw [Scheme.Opens.range_ι]
    exact hVzmem z
  · intro z
    refine ⟨iIdx (g.base z) (idx z).1 (idx z).2,
      (φ z).resLE (Vz z) ((φ z) ⁻¹ᵁ Vz z) le_rfl ≫ vz z ≫
        lMap (g.base z) (idx z).1 (idx z).2, ?_⟩
    simp only [Category.assoc, hlMap, reassoc_of% hvz z, Scheme.Hom.resLE_comp_ι_assoc,
      reassoc_of% hφb z, hpC]

end AlgebraicGeometry

